    "content" : "I finally ordered and received all of the parts needed to finish my CEE board. I only had to solder up the ATXmega microcontroller and the QFN-12-leaded op-amps. Using my hotplate and solder paste made soldering the uC easy work. I attempted to record the process but found out after it was finished that I didn&#39;t hit the record button on my phone (D&#39;oh!). The op-amps were much harder because the leads are located at the bottom of the package. I won&#39;t be sure until I can test it if they soldered correctly or not. I sure hope they worked. The only thing left to do is program it. After talking with the developers, I found out my current programmer won&#39;t program this atmel chip. Once I order a new programmer, I will be sure to post the results of my soldering.",
    "objectType" : "note",
    "originalContent" : "I finally ordered and received all of the parts needed to finish my CEE board. I only had to solder up the ATXmega microcontroller and the QFN-12-leaded op-amps. Using my hotplate and solder paste made soldering the uC easy work. I attempted to record the process but found out after it was finished that I didn't hit the record button on my phone (D'oh!). The op-amps were much harder because the leads are located at the bottom of the package. I won't be sure until I can test it if they soldered correctly or not. I sure hope they worked. The only thing left to do is program it. After talking with the developers, I found out my current programmer won't program this atmel chip. Once I order a new programmer, I will be sure to post the results of my soldering.",
